# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# runtime state — a privacy control, not tidiness. `__main__.py` defaults
# CHAT_GATEWAY_STATE_DIR to `state` and CHAT_GATEWAY_INBOX_DIR to `inbox-data`,
# and BOTH are relative to the working directory — so README's documented
# `python3 -m chat_gateway serve`, run from the repo root, writes them into the
# worktree, where `git add -A` will happily stage them. Both carry message
# content: `state/queue/*.jsonl` journals `message.model_dump()` — the whole
# outbound text and cards (delivery.py) — and `inbox-data/<app>-<day>.jsonl`
# holds an inbound reply's text, sender_email and raw event (inbox.py).
# Unanchored deliberately: the working directory is not knowable from here, and
# a `state/` one level down leaks exactly as much as one at the root. Deployment
# points both env vars at absolute paths outside any checkout; these patterns
# are the guard for local runs, not the mechanism.
# No .gitkeep placeholder: every writer already does
# `mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)`, so one would buy nothing and would put
# the directory back into the worktree it is being kept out of.
state/
inbox-data/
*.log

# design-asset verification dumps (generate_avatars.py --verify)
docs/assets/_verify/

